> Choose an order for the source magnitudes

For n<2^k, q=0, so every word has length k+1. Increasing k
therefore penalises very small values but can reduce the doubled
quotient prefix for large ones. No single order wins on every source.
For example zero costs one bit at order zero but 64 bits at order 63;
UINT64_MAX costs 129 bits at order zero and 66 at order 63.

We compare three controlled sequences: 128 zeros; 127 zeros followed
by 65535; and all integers 0..127. These inputs isolate magnitude
patterns without claiming a measured production distribution. Each plotted
point is an exact native size calculation and is checked against actual
encoding and decoding. Order selection is external; its transmission
cost is excluded. Nonempty all-zero sequences use one bit per field
under the explicitly positive-width fixed-field convention.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/exp_golomb_orders.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<std::uint64_t> zeros(128,0),rare=zeros,ramp;rare.back()=65535;for(std::uint64_t n=0;n<128;++n)ramp.push_back(n);
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::string,std::vector<std::uint64_t>>> inputs{{"zeros",zeros},{"rare large",rare},{"0..127",ramp}};
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{{37,99,235},{22,163,74},{124,58,237}};
  std::print("| fixture | N | order k | coded bits | positive fixed width | fixed bits | round trip |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<inputs.size();++i){const auto& [name,values]=inputs[i];std::vector<double>x,b;
    for(int k=0;k<=8;++k){const auto s=dm::algorithms::exp_golomb_size(values,k);const auto e=dm::algorithms::exp_golomb_encode_work(values,k);const auto d=dm::algorithms::exp_golomb_decode_work(e.bits,int(values.size()),k);
      if(s.bits!=e.bits.size()||d.values!=values||d.consumed_bits!=e.bits.size())throw std::runtime_error("size/codec mismatch");
      std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",name,s.values,k,s.bits,s.fixed_width,s.fixed_bits,d.values==values);x.push_back(k);b.push_back(s.bits);}
    p.line(x,b,name,colors[i]).points(x,b,"",colors[i],4);}
  p.title("The useful order depends on the magnitudes").x_label("Common order k (known to decoder)").y_label("Exact coded payload bits for N = 128").size(1000,540).save_svg("build/exp_golomb_orders.svg");
}
