> Measure actual work and optional retained history

For N copies of ten at order two, the kernel actually visits N zero
positions, 2N quotient positions and 2N low-bit positions, for B=5N.
These counters describe logical bit positions, excluding scalar preflight,
allocation, copies and validation; they are not CPU instruction counts.
Both encoding and parsing take O(N+B) time. Ordinary encoding owns
O(B) output, while decoding owns O(actual values) output and borrows
its input. Ordinary/work calls keep no optional word history.

A trace owns B bits, N value entries and N whole word records, so the
defined logical capture is C=B+2N=7N for this family. Scalar metadata,
capacity, runtime temporaries and allocator/container bytes are excluded;
C is not peak RAM. Encoding checks known C before copies or emission.
Decoding first reserves its whole input B, including any unread tail,
then two entries before each completed value/span append. The quota
defaults to one million; zero disables only this optional quota.
Checked arithmetic and container limits remain, and exceptions expose no
partial trace.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/exp_golomb_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::vector<double>x,zeros,quotient,low,visits,capture;
  std::print("| N | actual zeros | actual quotient | actual low bits | actual bit visits | encode capture | decode capture |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:std::vector<std::size_t>{0,1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128}){
    const std::vector<std::uint64_t> values(n,10);const auto e=dm::algorithms::exp_golomb_encode_trace(values,2);const auto d=dm::algorithms::exp_golomb_decode_trace(e.bits,int(n),2);
    if(d.values!=values||e.work.zero_prefix_bits!=n||e.work.quotient_bits!=2*n||e.work.suffix_bits!=2*n||e.work.bit_visits!=5*n||d.work.bit_visits!=5*n||e.captured_entries!=7*n||d.captured_entries!=7*n)throw std::runtime_error("actual linear work identity failed");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,e.work.zero_prefix_bits,e.work.quotient_bits,e.work.suffix_bits,e.work.bit_visits,e.captured_entries,d.captured_entries);
    x.push_back(n);zeros.push_back(e.work.zero_prefix_bits);quotient.push_back(e.work.quotient_bits);low.push_back(e.work.suffix_bits);visits.push_back(e.work.bit_visits);capture.push_back(e.captured_entries);}
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();a.line(x,zeros,"Zero prefix N",{37,99,235}).line(x,quotient,"Quotient 2N",{22,163,74}).points(x,low,"Low bits 2N",{234,88,12},4)
    .title("Actual field counts").x_label("Repeated values N").y_label("Bit positions");
  auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();b.line(x,visits,"Visited bits 5N",{37,99,235}).line(x,capture,"Capture entries 7N",{124,58,237})
    .title("Output and retained history").x_label("Repeated values N").y_label("Logical bits or entries");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,530).title("Repeated ten at order two: exact kernel and capture counts").fit_panels().save_svg("build/exp_golomb_work.svg");
}
