> Scope and reference

Short word boundaries solve integer delimiting for a known order. They
do not select a source model, choose the best order, frame a message,
or pack a byte stream. A complete codec must supply those layers.
The executed examples preserve the original nine codewords, eight-value
round trip and ten sampled lengths, while checking full-width arithmetic,
actual spans, distribution-dependent costs and malformed attempted words.

- ITU-T H.274 (05/2022), *Versatile supplemental enhancement information
  messages for coded video bitstreams*, section 9.1, equation (72) and
  Table 21. [Official English specification](https://www.itu.int/rec/dologin_pub.asp?id=T-REC-H.274-202205-S!!PDF-E&lang=e&type=items).
  The native API follows the unsigned order-k mathematical coding rule
  on uint64 with checked framing parameters and complete attempted words.
  Field-specific video syntax constraints, signed mappings, NAL framing
  and full video bitstream conformance are outside this API.

